{"slug": "enchantress", "nyt_id": 12534, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12534-enchantress", "name": "Enchantress", "author": "Jim Meehan", "description": "Your success with home mixology will be defined as much by what you stock as how you use it. Most home bars contain a decent selection of base spirits and very few modifiers. A bucket of ice, a few limes and a minibar may look like a world of opportunities, but it’s not. So instead of planning a party around what you have around the house, buy a modifier like orange Curaçao, Bénédictine, maraschino or Campari. You can make several different classic cocktails by pairing one of those with bitters, vermouth or a few items from the fruit stand. You’ll also build up your back bar, one bottle at a time.", "servings": {"text": "1 drink", "min": 1, "max": 1, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": null, "raw": {}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 ounces port", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "port", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ounce cognac", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "cognac", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ ounce orange Curaçao", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "orange curaçao", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "½ ounce lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "oz", "item": "lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Orange twist, for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "orange twist", "preparation": "for garnish", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Shake all liquid ingredients with ice. Strain into a rocks glass filled with ice. Garnish with an orange twist"}], "nu